  "contract": "Bridge adapter webhooks (BridgeAdapterController) as published Server 2.11.1 serves them, in their own namespace: the adapter name, payload and action refusals (422, the target redacted to its routing fields); start_workflow accepted (202), returned as a duplicate (200) under the default policy, rejected under reject_duplicate (422), with a workflow ID derived from the adapter and the idempotency key when none is given, and on the default queue for an unconfigured type; signal_workflow and update_workflow refused for an unknown workflow or a malformed target, accepted (202), and deduplicated (200) by adapter, action, idempotency key and target name. Run IDs are labels in order of first appearance and derived workflow IDs are checked against PHP's derivation. One published defect is bounded: a bridge update to an SDK-worker workflow skips external update admission and is rejected workflow_definition_unavailable; the published answers or the intended acceptance and deduplication are accepted. Embedded applications have no HTTP bridge adapters."
